cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite the archived release version and its DOI, as identified in the repository README and admission record."
title: "The Perron vector of a totient Gram matrix and its harmonic approximation"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Kline
    given-names: Jeffery
abstract: >-
  Let R_n be the n-by-n matrix whose (j,k) entry counts the integers up to
  j/k that are coprime to j, and let Q_n = R_n^T R_n be its Gram matrix. Kline
  (2020) showed Q_n mu_n = e_1 and conjectured that the Perron vector v_n of
  Q_n satisfies lim n || h_n - (v_n^T h_n) v_n ||_inf = 1 with h_n(k) = 1/k.
  This release proves the conjecture. The residual scaled by n converges
  coordinatewise to an explicit arithmetic profile U(n/k), and the conjecture
  reduces to |U(t)| <= 1 for real t >= 1, which is closed by an exact integer
  certificate for t <= 10^6 and an analytic tail bound below 0.68 based on
  Ramare's explicit harmonic Mobius estimate. The dominant eigenvalue has
  leading constant G/3, and v_n^T mu_n is asymptotic to 3 sqrt(6) n^-3 /(pi G),
  replacing the 2020 O(n^-3/2) bound. An exact convolution identity shows the
  eigenvector approximation yields no new estimate for the harmonic Mobius sum.
  A bounded literature search found no other resolution of the conjecture; this
  is a statement about the searched corpus, not a priority claim.
keywords:
  - Mobius function
  - Euler totient
  - truncated totient
  - dominant eigenvector
  - Perron vector
  - rank-one perturbation
  - computer-assisted proof
  - exact integer certificate
  - Mertens function
repository-code: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/truncated-totient-eigenvector"
url: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/truncated-totient-eigenvector"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
